468:\subsection{Degree-2 Elimination} 
472:        \label{red:degree-2}
473:        Given a graph $G = (V, E)$ and any node $x$ with degree 2, construct the elimination graph $G_x$. The potentially non-minimum ordering of $G$ is $x \Sigma(G_x)$. The reduction is applied recursively until no nodes with degree 2 are left.
