STEP 0 clears the family only on Track B. The paper’s Section 5 explicitly detects twins by hashing, sorting, and comparing neighborhoods (worst case \(O(mn+n\log n)\)); Track A would therefore be false. The retained family instead uses Theorem 4/Reduction 3’s exact twin object, with a planted three-vertex witness, a measured global row-sort route of about 32,000 operations per shipping instance, and a 236-operation rooted structural route. I found one current-spec bug: its self-test still gates on the retired hinted-oracle rule, so I’m correcting that before refreshing evidence.
Full-paper triage supports the existing native twin-reduction family as Track B, not the original Track-A minimum-fill hypothesis. I am auditing and repairing the retained implementation rather than discarding it.
