codex
Implemented and locally verified a native Track-B twin-reduction generator based on Theorem 4 and Reduction 3 of the [paper](https://arxiv.org/pdf/2004.11315).

The result is not yet shippable:

- All local G1–G9(c) gates pass.
- The named `hard` preset was solved by 3/3 oracle calls.
- Escalated `n=3600` was solved by 2/3.
- OpenRouter quota was exhausted at `n=5400`, so `harden.py` could not issue a final verdict or run the hinted/placebo diagnostics.
- API errors were not counted as failures.

Artifacts:

- [Generator](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2004.11315/gen_2004_11315.py)
- [Self-test report](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2004.11315/selftest_report.json)
- [README](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2004.11315/README.md)
- [Bare transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2004.11315/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [Hinted transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2004.11315/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl)
- [Placebo transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2004.11315/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)
- [Blocker details](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2004.11315/BLOCKED.md)

After replenishing the OpenRouter quota, resume with:

```bash
python3 ../../scripts/harden.py gen_2004_11315.py
```
